00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:27.090
In the Mundane World, he's
the supreme commander of the yokai,

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:30.470
but he doesn't really have any strong defining elements.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.310
Well... Uh...

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:40.440
I'm shy... and don't even know
why my status was elevated the way it was...

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.900
But it's okay, isn't it?

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.360
If I'm truly the supreme commander, I mean.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.240
Well, in reality I'm as you see me, though.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:54.040
In group photos, I was sure to be
the only one not visible in the frame.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:06:00.250
Certain people end up not having even a single photo
in the yearbook or from a field trip, you know?

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:05.760
I feel that all of those kinds of people are my kin.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:12.640
To think that a guy like you is meow the
supreme commander of Japan's yokai is kinda sad...

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:17.390
Well, you certainly do look the part
of a Japanese yokai, though.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:24.280
To spot me and pick me up like that,
you must be an unusual fellow.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:31.200
One aspect of Mr. Hozuki is that his eyes
are strangely drawn toward minute details...

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.240
When he cleans the bath,
he's the type of guy who uses a toothbrush

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.620
and focuses squarely on scrubbing
the nooks and crannies, you kn-

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:37.660
Hana
Kappo
Kitsune
Gozen

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:41.710
So, Nurarihyon, what was it you wanted
to tell me, anyway?

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:45.500
Ah, about the unpaid bill at the fox cafe...

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:49.050
That, uh, was me.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.550
SO YOU'RE THE ONE!

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.470
HOW DARE YOU DINE AND DASH, YOU LITTLE...!

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.060
You've got it wrong! All wrong!

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.560
I left money to cover my bill.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.770
No matter how much I tried to get the attention
of the staff, no one came to the cash register,

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.770
so I left it under the register...

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.110
"Under the register"?

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.360
Seems no one noticed...

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:11.740
Whenever I go to a shop,
this kind of thing always happens.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:15.080
Just like in this case,
they don't even recognize I've left money...

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:20.250
And when I try to order, they pass right by me
two or three times, you see.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:23.630
Uh, excuse me... Um...

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:29.800
Well, that's 'cause you're so timid and speak so quietly.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:34.050
So why meow did this guy start
to get called the supreme commander?

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:36.390
People can't get a clear picture of him,

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:40.180
so it's easy for their imaginations
to run wild... most likely.

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:45.270
It's nice, isn't it? That may be how they imagine me,
but it's actually also the appearance I long for.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.690
Ideal                  Reality

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:49.740
If you long to be like that,
mew outta act a bit more boldly.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:54.320
No, I could never! It's fine for the foxes
and nekomata to be like that, though.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:58.290
I mean, I'm not that significant
of a yokai myself, you know.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.160
Yokai                    Major
League               Ranked

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:02.120
